INSERT INTO `questions` VALUES (1,'HR','easy','Tell me about yourself.','I am a Computer Science student with a strong foundation in software engineering and web technologies. Over the past few years, I have built multiple full-stack projects, focused on clean architecture and problem solving. I enjoy tackling complex challenges and continuously upgrading my technical skills.','Follow the Present-Past-Future structure: what you do now, key background achievements, and what excites you about this role.','2026-10-05 06:33:24'),(2,'HR','medium','Why should we hire you over other candidates?','You should hire me because I offer a strong blend of technical fundamentals, quick learning agility, and a collaborative mindset. I don\'t just write code; I focus on delivering reliable, user-centered solutions and taking full ownership of project outcomes.','Highlight your unique combination of skills, work ethic, and cultural alignment with the team.','2026-10-05 06:33:24'),(3,'HR','easy','What are your greatest strengths?','My primary strengths are analytical problem solving, rapid adaptation to new tools and frameworks, and disciplined time management. I break complex requirements into modular tasks and execute them methodically.','Pick 2-3 specific strengths with brief concrete examples rather than generic buzzwords.','2026-10-05 06:33:24'),(4,'HR','medium','What is your greatest weakness, and how are you addressing it?','Early on, I struggled with perfectionism and spent too much time refining non-critical details. I addressed this by adopting agile estimation techniques, setting strict time-boxes for initial drafts, and gathering feedback early.','Always choose a genuine professional weakness and clearly emphasize the concrete steps you take to manage it.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(5,'HR','medium','Where do you see yourself in five years?','In five years, I aim to have deepened my technical expertise into senior engineering and system architecture. I want to take ownership of end-to-end technical decisions and mentor junior engineers while contributing to high-impact products.','Show ambition balanced with realistic milestones aligned with engineering growth.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(6,'HR','medium','Why do you want to work at this company?','I admire your team\'s commitment to engineering excellence, scalability, and solving real user problems. Having followed your product updates and architecture blog, I believe my background in modern web systems aligns directly with your mission.','Demonstrate that you researched their products, values, and engineering culture.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(7,'HR','hard','How do you handle high pressure or tight deadlines?','I manage pressure by stepping back to clarify priorities, breaking the workload into high-impact deliverables, and communicating transparently with stakeholders. Keeping a structured checklist and focusing on execution prevents panic.','Provide an example using the STAR method showing calm prioritization under stress.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(8,'HR','easy','Describe your ideal work environment.','I thrive in an environment that values transparent communication, continuous learning, and collaborative ownership. I appreciate teams where constructive code reviews and open feedback are encouraged.','Emphasize collaboration, engineering discipline, and a balance of autonomy and support.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(9,'HR','easy','What motivates you to do your best work?','I am motivated by solving difficult problems and seeing the tangible positive impact of my code on end users. Building robust, clean software that simplifies people\'s tasks is deeply rewarding for me.','Focus on intrinsic motivation such as craft quality, curiosity, and user impact.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(10,'HR','medium','How do you stay updated with emerging industry technologies?','I follow engineering blogs like Engineering at Uber and GitHub, read documentation for new language standards, experiment with side projects, and engage in developer communities.','Mention specific publications, newsletters, podcasts, or practical sandbox repositories.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(11,'HR','medium','Tell me about a time you had to learn a technology very quickly.','When our team needed to implement real-time messaging for a college project, none of us had worked with WebSockets. I spent a weekend studying the protocol, built a small proof of concept, and integrated it into our stack by the next sprint.','Highlight your learning methodology: documentation, small prototypes, and practical execution.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(12,'HR','medium','How do you handle receiving critical feedback on your work?','I view feedback as a crucial tool for technical and personal growth. I separate my ego from my work, listen carefully to understand the reviewer\'s perspective, ask clarifying questions, and implement the recommended improvements.','Show emotional maturity and a growth mindset.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(13,'HR','medium','Tell me about a project you are particularly proud of.','I am proud of an automated mock interview simulator I developed with persistent storage and AI answer evaluation. I engineered the full pipeline from database schema design to external API integrations and responsive UI.','Focus on technical challenges solved, personal contributions, and measurable results.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(14,'HR','medium','How do you prioritize competing deadlines?','I evaluate tasks based on business impact and dependencies using an urgency-importance matrix. I keep stakeholders informed early if a deadline requires scope adjustment rather than silently slipping.','Mention transparency and proactive communication alongside prioritization criteria.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(15,'HR','medium','What are your salary expectations for this position?','Based on my research into market benchmarks for entry-level software engineering roles in this location and my technical skill set, I am looking for a competitive package in the standard industry range. I am open to discussing this further based on the total compensation structure.','Give a researched range or defer politely until scope and responsibilities are fully outlined.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(16,'HR','easy','HR Question 16: How do you approach handling burnout risk in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing handling burnout risk, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I monitor my focus levels, enforce clear boundaries between work and rest, and communicate early with leads if workload volume begins compromising code quality.','Show proactive health and energy management.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(17,'HR','medium','HR Question 17: How do you approach ethical dilemmas in software development in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing ethical dilemmas in software development, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. In any situation involving data privacy or security shortcuts, I advocate for user protection and transparent compliance with technical standards, escalating concerns professionally.','Emphasize integrity and user trust.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(18,'HR','hard','HR Question 18: How do you approach managing remote work effectively in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing managing remote work effectively, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. Remote work requires clear asynchronous documentation, punctual participation in syncs, and proactive status updates to maintain team alignment.','Highlight written communication and self-discipline.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(19,'HR','easy','HR Question 19: How do you approach mentoring peers or juniors in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing mentoring peers or juniors, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I focus on guiding colleagues to discover solutions rather than simply giving answers, fostering their problem-solving independence and confidence.','Show empathy, patience, and structured guidance.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(20,'HR','medium','HR Question 20: How do you approach celebrating team success vs individual credit in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing celebrating team success vs individual credit, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. Software is a team sport. I always ensure collective efforts are recognized and acknowledge peers who contributed to unblocking the project.','Show humility and team-first orientation.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(21,'HR','hard','HR Question 21: How do you approach cultural fit and company values in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing cultural fit and company values, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. Aligning personal values with company culture ensures long-term mutual growth. I research company values and ensure my everyday communication and work ethics mirror those standards.','Be authentic and reference specific corporate values.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(22,'HR','easy','HR Question 22: How do you approach handling ambiguous instructions in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing handling ambiguous instructions, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. When given ambiguous requirements, I document my assumptions, create a minimal prototype, and schedule a quick sync to validate the direction before committing deep effort.','Show initiative in seeking clarity without being paralyzed.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(23,'HR','medium','HR Question 23: How do you approach dealing with repetitive tasks in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing dealing with repetitive tasks, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I approach repetitive tasks by standardizing them and writing automation scripts where possible. If automation isn\'t feasible, I focus on accuracy and consistency.','Highlight an automation mindset and discipline.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(24,'HR','hard','HR Question 24: How do you approach presenting technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing presenting technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I avoid jargon, use concrete analogies, and focus on business outcomes and user impact rather than low-level implementation details.','Focus on empathy for the audience and clarity.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(25,'HR','easy','HR Question 25: How do you approach disagreeing with a team decision in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing disagreeing with a team decision, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I voice my perspective with objective data during the discussion phase. Once the team reaches a consensus, I commit fully to the agreed direction even if it differed from my initial preference.','Demonstrate the \'disagree and commit\' principle.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(26,'HR','medium','HR Question 26: How do you approach handling burnout risk in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing handling burnout risk, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I monitor my focus levels, enforce clear boundaries between work and rest, and communicate early with leads if workload volume begins compromising code quality.','Show proactive health and energy management.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(27,'HR','hard','HR Question 27: How do you approach ethical dilemmas in software development in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing ethical dilemmas in software development, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. In any situation involving data privacy or security shortcuts, I advocate for user protection and transparent compliance with technical standards, escalating concerns professionally.','Emphasize integrity and user trust.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(28,'HR','easy','HR Question 28: How do you approach managing remote work effectively in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing managing remote work effectively, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. Remote work requires clear asynchronous documentation, punctual participation in syncs, and proactive status updates to maintain team alignment.','Highlight written communication and self-discipline.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(29,'HR','medium','HR Question 29: How do you approach mentoring peers or juniors in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing mentoring peers or juniors, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I focus on guiding colleagues to discover solutions rather than simply giving answers, fostering their problem-solving independence and confidence.','Show empathy, patience, and structured guidance.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(30,'HR','hard','HR Question 30: How do you approach celebrating team success vs individual credit in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing celebrating team success vs individual credit, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. Software is a team sport. I always ensure collective efforts are recognized and acknowledge peers who contributed to unblocking the project.','Show humility and team-first orientation.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(31,'HR','easy','HR Question 31: How do you approach cultural fit and company values in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing cultural fit and company values, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. Aligning personal values with company culture ensures long-term mutual growth. I research company values and ensure my everyday communication and work ethics mirror those standards.','Be authentic and reference specific corporate values.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(32,'HR','medium','HR Question 32: How do you approach handling ambiguous instructions in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing handling ambiguous instructions, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. When given ambiguous requirements, I document my assumptions, create a minimal prototype, and schedule a quick sync to validate the direction before committing deep effort.','Show initiative in seeking clarity without being paralyzed.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(33,'HR','hard','HR Question 33: How do you approach dealing with repetitive tasks in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing dealing with repetitive tasks, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I approach repetitive tasks by standardizing them and writing automation scripts where possible. If automation isn\'t feasible, I focus on accuracy and consistency.','Highlight an automation mindset and discipline.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(34,'HR','easy','HR Question 34: How do you approach presenting technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing presenting technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I avoid jargon, use concrete analogies, and focus on business outcomes and user impact rather than low-level implementation details.','Focus on empathy for the audience and clarity.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(35,'HR','medium','HR Question 35: How do you approach disagreeing with 