l responsibility and open communication. I monitor my focus levels, enforce clear boundaries between work and rest, and communicate early with leads if workload volume begins compromising code quality.','Show proactive health and energy management.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(67,'HR','easy','HR Question 67: How do you approach ethical dilemmas in software development in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing ethical dilemmas in software development, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. In any situation involving data privacy or security shortcuts, I advocate for user protection and transparent compliance with technical standards, escalating concerns professionally.','Emphasize integrity and user trust.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(68,'HR','medium','HR Question 68: How do you approach managing remote work effectively in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing managing remote work effectively, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. Remote work requires clear asynchronous documentation, punctual participation in syncs, and proactive status updates to maintain team alignment.','Highlight written communication and self-discipline.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(69,'HR','hard','HR Question 69: How do you approach mentoring peers or juniors in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing mentoring peers or juniors, my approach is grounded in professional responsibility and open communication. I focus on guiding colleagues to discover solutions rather than simply giving answers, fostering their problem-solving independence and confidence.','Show empathy, patience, and structured guidance.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(70,'HR','easy','HR Question 70: How do you approach celebrating team success vs individual credit in a collaborative software engineering environment?','When managing celebrating team success vs individual credit, my approac