ial for stability and scale. CSS specificity determines which rule takes precedence when multiple selectors target an element. It is calculated based on inline styles (1000), IDs (100), classes/attributes/pseudo-classes (10), and elements/pseudo-elements (1).','Explain the specificity calculation order.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(193,'Technical','hard','Technical Question 93: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) prevention.','In modern web systems, Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) prevention is essential for stability and scale. XSS occurs when malicious scripts are injected into trusted websites. Prevention requires sanitizing and escaping user input, implementing Content Security Policy (CSP), and avoiding unsafe APIs like innerHTML.','Distinguish between stored, reflected, and DOM-based XSS.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(194,'Technical','easy','Technical Question 94: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) tokens.','In modern web systems, Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) tokens is essential for stability and scale. CSRF tricks an authenticated user into executing unwanted actions. It is prevented using anti-CSRF synchronizer tokens validated on state-changing requests and using SameSite cookie attributes.','Explain the mechanism of forged requests and token verification.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(195,'Technical','medium','Technical Question 95: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of database normalization and normal forms.','In modern web systems, database normalization and normal forms is essential for stability and scale. Database normalization organizes tables to reduce data redundancy and eliminate anomalies. 1NF requires atomic values, 2NF eliminates partial dependencies, and 3NF eliminates transitive dependencies.','Explain 1NF, 2NF, and 3NF simply.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(196,'Technical','hard','Technical Question 96: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of session management vs JWT authentication.','In modern web systems, session management vs JWT authentication is essential for stability and scale. Session-based auth stores session data server-side (in memory or database) with a session ID cookie. JWT stores signed claims inside a token client-side, enabling stateless authentication across distributed microservices.','Contrast server memory overhead with token invalidation challenges.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(197,'Technical','easy','Technical Question 97: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of HTTP/1.1 vs HTTP/2 and multiplexing.','In modern web systems, HTTP/1.1 vs HTTP/2 and multiplexing is essential for stability and scale. HTTP/1.1 suffers from head-of-line blocking and opens multiple TCP connections. HTTP/2 introduces binary framing, request multiplexing over a single TCP connection, header compression (HPACK), and server push.','Focus on multiplexing and single TCP connection benefits.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(198,'Technical','medium','Technical Question 98: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of web caching strategies and Cache-Control headers.','In modern web systems, web caching strategies and Cache-Control headers is essential for stability and scale. Web caching reduces latency and server load. The Cache-Control header directives (max-age, no-cache, no-store, immutable) combined with ETags govern browser and CDN caching lifetimes.','Explain max-age, ETag validation, and CDN edge caching.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(199,'Technical','hard','Technical Question 99: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of WebSocket protocol vs long polling.','In modern web systems, WebSocket protocol vs long polling is essential for stability and scale. WebSockets provide persistent, full-duplex bidirectional communication over a single TCP connection with minimal overhead. Long polling repeatedly opens HTTP requests, incurring substantial header latency.','Contrast bidirectional full-duplex sockets with unidirectional HTTP polling.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(200,'Technical','easy','Technical Question 100: Explain the core architecture and practical implementation of frontend performance optimization techniques.','In modern web systems, frontend performance optimization techniques is essential for stability and scale. Optimizations include code splitting, lazy loading images and components, minifying assets, tree shaking, critical CSS inlining, and optimizing Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS).','Highlight measurable performance metrics and asset bundling techniques.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(201,'Behavioral','medium','Tell me about a time you faced a difficult technical challenge and how you solved it.','In our academic database project, queries began timing out as table rows grew into thousands. I investigated the execution plans using EXPLAIN, identified missing composite indexes on foreign keys, and restructured the query joins, reducing query latency by over 80%.','Use STAR (Situation, Task, Action, Result) with clear technical metrics.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(202,'Behavioral','medium','Describe a time you had a disagreement with a team member. How did you resolve it?','During a hackathon, a teammate wanted to build custom authentication from scratch while I recommended using an established OAuth library to save time. I drafted a pros-and-cons document with time estimates. We agreed on OAuth for MVP, which allowed us to finish core features before the deadline.','Focus on objective data, mutual respect, and prioritizing project goals.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(203,'Behavioral','hard','Tell me about a time you failed to meet a deadline. What happened and what did you learn?','During a course milestone, I underestimated the complexity of third-party API integration and fell behind schedule. I notified my instructor 48 hours early, presented a working core feature set, and submitted the completed integration two days later. Since then, I build a 20% buffer into all estimation plans.','Own the failure directly, highlight proactive communication, and explain what preventive process you established.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(204,'Behavioral','easy','Describe a situation where you had to adapt quickly to significant change.','Midway through a semester project, our backend partner had to drop the course for medical reasons. I volunteered to take over backend API development alongside my frontend duties, learned Express.js within three days, and delivered the required endpoints on time.','Show adaptability, resilience, and willingness to step up for the team.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(205,'Behavioral','easy','Tell me about a time you received constructive criticism. How did you handle it?','During a senior code review, my mentor noted that my commit history was disorganized and lacked automated tests. Rather than feeling defensive, I asked for their recommended Git branching workflow, studied test-driven practices, and adopted strict commit conventions across all subsequent PRs.','Demonstrate humility, listening ability, and measurable action taken.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(206,'Behavioral','medium','Describe a time you demonstrated leadership, even if you were not the formal leader.','In a collaborative lab assignment, our team was stalled because tasks were ambiguously defined. I proposed a quick standup, created a shared Trello board, broken tasks into distinct tickets with owners, and established a daily integration check, guiding the team to a top grade.','Leadership is about facilitating progress and helping others succeed.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(207,'Behavioral','hard','Tell me about a time you had to deal with an unhappy stakeholder or client.','In a freelance project, a client was disappointed that a feature was not behaving as expected. I scheduled a video walkthrough, listened without interrupting to identify the root misunderstanding, clarified the scope, and delivered a customized configuration option within 24 hours.','Show active listening, professional empathy, and prompt corrective action.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(208,'Behavioral','medium','Describe a project where you had to balance competing priorities.','During finals week, I had to prepare for two critical exams while finalizing our semester PBL web project. I created an hourly schedule, automated repetitive deployment scripts to save manual testing hours, and coordinated with my project partner to divide testing duties cleanly.','Demonstrate systematic time management and disciplined follow-through.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(209,'Behavioral','easy','Tell me about a time you noticed a mistake in your work before anyone else did.','While reviewing my pull request before merging, I realized I had left test API keys hardcoded in an environment configuration file. I immediately revoked the key, rotated credentials, migrated secrets to a local .env file, and added gitignore rules to prevent recurrence.','Highlight integrity, attention to detail, and systemic remediation.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(210,'Behavioral','medium','Describe a situation where you motivated an unmotivated peer.','A peer on our project was disengaged because they felt overwhelmed by the framework learning curve. I paired with them for two hours to build a working \'Hello World\' module together and assigned them a bite-sized component. Gaining momentum restored their confidence and enthusiasm.','Show empathy, mentorship, and practical support to build momentum.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(211,'Behavioral','medium','Behavioral Question 11: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in handling unexpected production bugs under pressure.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing handling unexpected production bugs under pressure was vital. When a bug emerged during live presentation, I stayed calm, inspected browser developer logs, identified a missing CORS header, applied a hotfix, and documented the root cause in our post-mortem.','Show emotional control and methodical troubleshooting.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(212,'Behavioral','hard','Behavioral Question 12: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in collaborating with cross-functional partners.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing collaborating with cross-functional partners was vital. I align early with design and product partners by translating visual wireframes into technical specifications and clarifying constraints before development starts.','Emphasize mutual respect and shared terminology.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(213,'Behavioral','easy','Behavioral Question 13: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in delivering quality work under tight constraints.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing delivering quality work under tight constraints was vital. When time is constrained, I focus on the critical path: building high-value user flows thoroughly rather than spreading effort thinly over half-finished features.','Highlight ruthless prioritization and high craft standards.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(214,'Behavioral','medium','Behavioral Question 14: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in admitting a lack of knowledge on a topic.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing admitting a lack of knowledge on a topic was vital. When asked about a framework I hadn\'t used, I answered honestly that I hadn\'t worked with it yet, explained related concepts I was proficient in, and outlined how quickly I could get up to speed.','Integrity and confidence in learning ability always beat bluffing.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(215,'Behavioral','hard','Behavioral Question 15: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in driving consensus among differing opinions.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing driving consensus among differing opinions was vital. I facilitate consensus by steering debates away from opinions toward testable hypotheses and prototype benchmarks that provide objective evidence.','Show data-driven decision making and diplomacy.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(216,'Behavioral','easy','Behavioral Question 16: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in navigating ambiguous product requirements.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing navigating ambiguous product requirements was vital. I write user stories, sketch flowcharts, and confirm acceptance criteria with stakeholders before implementing complex workflows.','Highlight proactive documentation and alignment.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(217,'Behavioral','medium','Behavioral Question 17: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in handling a teammate who wasn\'t pulling their weight.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing handling a teammate who wasn\'t pulling their weight was vital. I initiated a private conversation to understand if they were facing personal or technical blockers, offered support on their first task, and agreed on daily check-ins to rebuild accountability.','Show compassion combined with healthy boundaries.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(218,'Behavioral','hard','Behavioral Question 18: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in learning from a failed experiment.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing learning from a failed experiment was vital. We experimented with an experimental caching library that introduced memory leaks. We reverted to standard HTTP caching, conducted a retrospective, and established benchmarking criteria before adopting new libraries.','Frame failure as an empirical learning milestone.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(219,'Behavioral','easy','Behavioral Question 19: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in prioritizing security and quality over speed.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing prioritizing security and quality over speed was vital. When pressured to skip input validation to hit a deadline, I explained the severity of injection vulnerabilities to the team lead and demonstrated that implementing parameterized queries took under an hour.','Show principled engineering ethics.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(220,'Behavioral','medium','Behavioral Question 20: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in celebrating peer achievements.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing celebrating peer achievements was vital. I make a conscious effort to acknowledge team members in public channels whenever they solve tricky bugs or deliver complex features on time.','Highlight a supportive team culture.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(221,'Behavioral','hard','Behavioral Question 21: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in handling unexpected production bugs under pressure.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing handling unexpected production bugs under pressure was vital. When a bug emerged during live presentation, I stayed calm, inspected browser developer logs, identified a missing CORS header, applied a hotfix, and documented the root cause in our post-mortem.','Show emotional control and methodical troubleshooting.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(222,'Behavioral','easy','Behavioral Question 22: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in collaborating with cross-functional partners.','In a project demanding high collaboration, addressing collaborating with cross-functional partners was vital. I align early with design and product partners by translating visual wireframes into technical specifications and clarifying constraints before development starts.','Emphasize mutual respect and shared terminology.','2026-10-05 06:33:25'),(223,'Behavioral','medium','Behavioral Question 23: Describe a scenario where you demonstrated excellence in delivering quality work under tight constraints.','In a project demanding high collaboration, 